      "publisher": "VoronDesign",
      "accessed": "2026-10-04",
      "supports": "p. 10 (Introduction, Blind joint basics): a BHCS in one extrusion's end, its head slid into the other extrusion's channel and tightened through an access hole; p. 14 (Frame): M5x16 BHCS in both ends of the 8 A extrusions; p. 15 (Frame assembly): the frame is joined by blind joints"
    }
  ],
  "frame_convention": "Origin at the centre of end A's cut face, on the extrusion axis. +z runs along the extrusion toward end B, whose face is at z = length_mm. +x and +y are normal to two adjacent slotted faces; the four faces sit at x = ±10 and y = ±10. Each face carries two slot interfaces on its centreline, at slot_station_mm from end A and from end B; their x_axis runs along the extrusion (+z). For blind joints, each end also carries a male end_a_blind / end_b_blind (the tapped end with its M5 button head, framed on the end face) and each face two female blind stations (blind_{face}_a / _b) on its centreline at blind_station_mm from end A and from end B, normal out of the face, x_axis along the extrusion.",
